    {
      "id": "p0259-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "This line is a two-pronged play on the English proverb \"curiosity killed the cat\". It contains a comical rhyme on the classic proverb, and it points to the fact that Mad Mew Mew has been possessed by the spirit of Mad Dummy.",
        "raw": "This line is a two-pronged play on the English proverb \"curiosity killed the cat\".\nIt contains a comical rhyme on the classic proverb, and it points to the fact that\nMad Mew Mew has been possessed by the spirit of Mad Dummy.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09594601,
          0.36409286,
          0.70690291,
          0.41327857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09212722,
          0.36337857,
          0.7089288,
          0.41435
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          12,
          13,
          14
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "这句话从两处改写了英语谚语“curiosity killed the cat”（好奇心害死猫）：用怒气的 Furiosity 换掉好奇心 curiosity，用驱使的 wills 换掉害死的 killed。它既俏皮地呼应原谚语的音韵，也点出了 Mad Mew Mew 被 Mad Dummy 的灵魂附身。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
