    {
      "id": "p0259-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In this situation, namennayo could be translated as \"don't screw with me\" - it's the sort of thing you'd hear from a tough guy about to start a fight. The phrase comes from the word nameru, which can mean \"to belittle\" in some contexts and \"to lick\" in more ordinary situations. This line is also a reference to namennayo, a slogan of the Nameneko brand of cat-related entertainment.",
        "raw": "In this situation, namennayo could be translated as \"don't screw with me\" - it's\nthe sort of thing you'd hear from a tough guy about to start a fight. The phrase\ncomes from the word nameru, which can mean \"to belittle\" in some contexts\nand \"to lick\" in more ordinary situations. This line is also a reference to\nnamennayo, a slogan of the Nameneko brand of cat-related entertainment.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
