    {
      "id": "p0259-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In the early 1980s, a Japanese photographer became famous for his photos of cats acting like tough ruffians. These photos exploded in popularity and were packaged into books and merchandise under the Nameneko brand name. The Nameneko fad was so big that the brand was even released internationally, under names like \"Pelorian\" and \"Don't Pelorian\".",
        "raw": "In the early 1980s, a Japanese photographer became famous for his photos\nof cats acting like tough ruffians. These photos exploded in popularity and\nwere packaged into books and merchandise under the Nameneko brand\nname. The Nameneko fad was so big that the brand was even released\ninternationally, under names like \"Pelorian\" and \"Don't Pelorian\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
